<DIV><IMG ALT="" border=0 DEFANGED_SRC="cid:lrwadg3j8ae6@supdie.com"></a><BR>Your barking up the wrong tree.A thorn in my side.  Play a harp before a cow.Sitting on the fence.Treat him like dirt.Strong as an ox. Sweet as honey.  Sow much, reap much; sow little, reap little.You feel like a fish out of water.What goes up must come down.A rose is a rose is a rose.What goes down usually comes up. Plain as water.You have to separate the chaff from the wheat.A weed is no more than a flower in disguise. Putting the cart before the horse.The shoes on the other foot now.  Turn over a new leaf.Sow dry and set wet.A place in the sun.  A thing of beauty is a joy forever.  The stronger the breeze the stronger the trees.Put that in your pipe and smoke it.  Spaceship earth.  They're like two peas in a pod. This is for the birds.  Timing is everything. Red as a beet. 
